{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 11, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 17, "tex": "\\section{Introduction}"}, {"line": 18, "tex": "\\label{section-introduction}"}, {"line": 20, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 21, "tex": "A reference is the lectures by Serre in the Seminaire Cartan, see"}, {"line": 22, "tex": "\\cite{Serre-Cartan}. Serre in turn refers to"}, {"line": 23, "tex": "\\cite{Deuring} and \\cite{ANT}. We changed some of the proofs, in particular"}, {"line": 24, "tex": "we used a fun argument of Rieffel to prove Wedderburn's theorem."}, {"line": 25, "tex": "Very likely this change is not an improvement and we strongly"}, {"line": 26, "tex": "encourage the reader to read the original exposition by Serre."}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 28, "section_label": "section-introduction", "section_start_line": 17, "section_title": "Introduction", "source_file": "brauer.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": []}
{"candidate_ids": [], "chapter_number": 11, "locally_named_context_leads": [{"kind": "definition", "label": "definition-finite", "line": 39}, {"kind": "definition", "label": "definition-skew-field", "line": 45}, {"kind": "definition", "label": "definition-simple", "line": 58}, {"kind": "definition", "label": "definition-central", "line": 67}, {"kind": "definition", "label": "definition-opposite", "line": 73}], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 0, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 29, "tex": "\\section{Noncommutative algebras}"}, {"line": 30, "tex": "\\label{section-algebras}"}, {"line": 32, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 33, "tex": "Let $k$ be a field. In this chapter an {\\it algebra} $A$ over $k$ is"}, {"line": 34, "tex": "a possibly noncommutative ring $A$ together with a ring map"}, {"line": 35, "tex": "$k \\to A$ such that $k$ maps into the center of $A$ and such that"}, {"line": 36, "tex": "$1$ maps to an identity element of $A$. An {\\it $A$-module} is a right"}, {"line": 37, "tex": "$A$-module such that the identity of $A$ acts as the identity."}, {"line": 39, "tex": "\\begin{definition}"}, {"line": 40, "tex": "\\label{definition-finite}"}, {"line": 41, "tex": "Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra. We say $A$ is {\\it finite} if $\\dim_k(A) < \\infty$."}, {"line": 42, "tex": "In this case we write $[A : k] = \\dim_k(A)$."}, {"line": 43, "tex": "\\end{definition}"}, {"line": 45, "tex": "\\begin{definition}"}, {"line": 46, "tex": "\\label{definition-skew-field}"}, {"line": 47, "tex": "A {\\it skew field} is a possibly noncommutative ring with an identity"}, {"line": 48, "tex": "element $1$, with $1 \\not = 0$, in which every nonzero element"}, {"line": 49, "tex": "has a multiplicative inverse."}, {"line": 50, "tex": "\\end{definition}"}, {"line": 52, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 53, "tex": "A skew field is a $k$-algebra for some $k$ (e.g., for the prime field"}, {"line": 54, "tex": "contained in it). We will use below that any module over a skew field"}, {"line": 55, "tex": "is free because a maximal linearly independent set of vectors forms a"}, {"line": 56, "tex": "basis and exists by Zorn's lemma."}, {"line": 58, "tex": "\\begin{definition}"}, {"line": 59, "tex": "\\label{definition-simple}"}, {"line": 60, "tex": "Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra."}, {"line": 61, "tex": "We say an $A$-module $M$ is {\\it simple} if it is nonzero and"}, {"line": 62, "tex": "the only $A$-submodules are $0$ and $M$."}, {"line": 63, "tex": "We say $A$ is {\\it simple} if the only two-sided ideals of $A$ are"}, {"line": 64, "tex": "$0$ and $A$."}, {"line": 65, "tex": "\\end{definition}"}, {"line": 67, "tex": "\\begin{definition}"}, {"line": 68, "tex": "\\label{definition-central}"}, {"line": 69, "tex": "A $k$-algebra $A$ is {\\it central} if the center of $A$ is the image of"}, {"line": 70, "tex": "$k \\to A$."}, {"line": 71, "tex": "\\end{definition}"}, {"line": 73, "tex": "\\begin{definition}"}, {"line": 74, "tex": "\\label{definition-opposite}"}, {"line": 75, "tex": "Given a $k$-algebra $A$ we denote $A^{op}$ the $k$-algebra we get by"}, {"line": 76, "tex": "reversing the order of multiplication in $A$. This is called the"}, {"line": 77, "tex": "{\\it opposite algebra}."}, {"line": 78, "tex": "\\end{definition}"}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 82, "section_label": "section-algebras", "section_start_line": 29, "section_title": "Noncommutative algebras", "source_file": "brauer.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": [{"environment": "definition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 39, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 43, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 45, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 50, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 58, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 65, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 67, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 71, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 73, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["definition"]}, {"environment": "definition", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 78, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["definition"]}]}
{"candidate_ids": ["candidate.stacks.d4fa96a82adc1f3f715f773c", "candidate.stacks.abc0c3a569a88bc97bf4978a", "candidate.stacks.d086d3c9d06c46ce914c8425"], "chapter_number": 11, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 38, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 83, "tex": "\\section{Wedderburn's theorem}"}, {"line": 84, "tex": "\\label{section-wedderburn}"}, {"line": 86, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 87, "tex": "The following cute argument can be found in a paper of Rieffel, see"}, {"line": 88, "tex": "\\cite{Rieffel}. The proof could not be simpler (quote from"}, {"line": 89, "tex": "Carl Faith's review)."}, {"line": 91, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 92, "tex": "\\label{lemma-rieffel}"}, {"line": 93, "tex": "Let $A$ be a possibly noncommutative ring with $1$ which contains no"}, {"line": 94, "tex": "nontrivial two-sided ideal. Let $M$ be a nonzero right ideal in $A$,"}, {"line": 95, "tex": "and view $M$ as a right $A$-module. Then $A$ coincides with the"}, {"line": 96, "tex": "bicommutant of $M$."}, {"line": 97, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 119, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 120, "tex": "\\label{lemma-simple-module}"}, {"line": 121, "tex": "Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra. If $A$ is finite, then"}, {"line": 122, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 123, "tex": "\\item $A$ has a simple module,"}, {"line": 124, "tex": "\\item any nonzero module contains a simple submodule,"}, {"line": 125, "tex": "\\item a simple module over $A$ has finite dimension over $k$, and"}, {"line": 126, "tex": "\\item if $M$ is a simple $A$-module, then $\\text{End}_A(M)$ is a"}, {"line": 127, "tex": "skew field."}, {"line": 128, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 129, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 140, "tex": "\\begin{theorem}"}, {"line": 141, "tex": "\\label{theorem-wedderburn}"}, {"line": 142, "tex": "\\begin{slogan}"}, {"line": 143, "tex": "Simple finite algebras over a field are matrix algebras over a skew field."}, {"line": 144, "tex": "\\end{slogan}"}, {"line": 145, "tex": "Let $A$ be a simple finite $k$-algebra. Then $A$ is a matrix algebra over"}, {"line": 146, "tex": "a finite $k$-algebra $K$ which is a skew field."}, {"line": 147, "tex": "\\end{theorem}"}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 165, "section_label": "section-wedderburn", "section_start_line": 83, "section_title": "Wedderburn's theorem", "source_file": "brauer.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": [{"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 91, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 91, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 97, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 99, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 119, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 119, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 129, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 131, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "theorem", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 140, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["theorem"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 140, "scope_stack": ["theorem"]}, {"environment": "theorem", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 147, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["theorem"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 149, "scope_stack": []}]}
{"candidate_ids": ["candidate.stacks.048b71183e0c82d13cd671a0", "candidate.stacks.3594d004ff5d1fc6deddb5b6", "candidate.stacks.627bb881641a6b0d4527d798", "candidate.stacks.4eb9aefba5727c50891e93d1", "candidate.stacks.3e3edd2864c576dac0f0413b", "candidate.stacks.f50c4090ab2b50842e411cbd", "candidate.stacks.b2fa9573cda3db3048521d61", "candidate.stacks.cf9b133ff8a985dad6693c78", "candidate.stacks.770144873366f2d8b67c69bc", "candidate.stacks.731172a8d8a595af253c0d99"], "chapter_number": 11, "locally_named_context_leads": [], "no_ambient_hypotheses_inferred": true, "omitted_proof_line_count": 100, "possible_scope_prose_line_numbers": [], "previous_draft_artifact_hint": null, "proof_free_source_lines": [{"line": 166, "tex": "\\section{Lemmas on algebras}"}, {"line": 167, "tex": "\\label{section-lemmas}"}, {"line": 169, "tex": "\\noindent"}, {"line": 170, "tex": "Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra. Let $B \\subset A$ be a subalgebra."}, {"line": 171, "tex": "The {\\it centralizer of $B$ in $A$} is the subalgebra"}, {"line": 172, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 173, "tex": "C  = \\{y \\in A \\mid xy = yx \\text{ for all }x \\in B\\}."}, {"line": 174, "tex": "$$"}, {"line": 175, "tex": "It is a $k$-algebra."}, {"line": 177, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 178, "tex": "\\label{lemma-centralizer}"}, {"line": 179, "tex": "Let $A$, $A'$ be $k$-algebras. Let $B \\subset A$, $B' \\subset A'$ be"}, {"line": 180, "tex": "subalgebras with centralizers $C$, $C'$. Then the centralizer of"}, {"line": 181, "tex": "$B \\otimes_k B'$ in $A \\otimes_k A'$ is $C \\otimes_k C'$."}, {"line": 182, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 192, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 193, "tex": "\\label{lemma-center-csa}"}, {"line": 194, "tex": "Let $A$ be a finite simple $k$-algebra. Then the center $k'$ of $A$"}, {"line": 195, "tex": "is a finite field extension of $k$."}, {"line": 196, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 208, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 209, "tex": "\\label{lemma-generate-two-sided-sub}"}, {"line": 210, "tex": "Let $V$ be a $k$ vector space. Let $K$ be a central $k$-algebra"}, {"line": 211, "tex": "which is a skew field. Let $W \\subset V \\otimes_k K$ be a two-sided"}, {"line": 212, "tex": "$K$-sub vector space. Then $W$ is generated as a left $K$-vector"}, {"line": 213, "tex": "space by $W \\cap (V \\otimes 1)$."}, {"line": 214, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 245, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 246, "tex": "\\label{lemma-generate-two-sided-ideal}"}, {"line": 247, "tex": "Let $A$ be a $k$-algebra. Let $K$ be a central $k$-algebra"}, {"line": 248, "tex": "which is a skew field. Then any two-sided ideal $I \\subset A \\otimes_k K$"}, {"line": 249, "tex": "is of the form $J \\otimes_k K$ for some two-sided ideal $J \\subset A$."}, {"line": 250, "tex": "In particular, if $A$ is simple, then so is $A \\otimes_k K$."}, {"line": 251, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 259, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 260, "tex": "\\label{lemma-matrix-algebras}"}, {"line": 261, "tex": "Let $R$ be a possibly noncommutative ring. Let $n \\geq 1$ be an integer."}, {"line": 262, "tex": "Let $R_n = \\text{Mat}(n \\times n, R)$."}, {"line": 263, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 264, "tex": "\\item The functors $M \\mapsto M^{\\oplus n}$ and"}, {"line": 265, "tex": "$N \\mapsto Ne_{11}$ define quasi-inverse equivalences of categories"}, {"line": 266, "tex": "$\\text{Mod}_R \\leftrightarrow \\text{Mod}_{R_n}$."}, {"line": 267, "tex": "\\item A two-sided ideal of $R_n$ is of the form $IR_n$ for some"}, {"line": 268, "tex": "two-sided ideal $I$ of $R$."}, {"line": 269, "tex": "\\item The center of $R_n$ is equal to the center of $R$."}, {"line": 270, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 271, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 280, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 281, "tex": "\\label{lemma-simple-module-unique}"}, {"line": 282, "tex": "Let $A$ be a finite simple $k$-algebra."}, {"line": 283, "tex": "\\begin{enumerate}"}, {"line": 284, "tex": "\\item There exists exactly one simple $A$-module $M$ up to isomorphism."}, {"line": 285, "tex": "\\item Any finite $A$-module is a direct sum of copies of a simple module."}, {"line": 286, "tex": "\\item Two finite $A$-modules are isomorphic if and only if they"}, {"line": 287, "tex": "have the same dimension over $k$."}, {"line": 288, "tex": "\\item If $A = \\text{Mat}(n \\times n, K)$ with $K$ a finite skew field"}, {"line": 289, "tex": "extension of $k$, then $M = K^{\\oplus n}$ is a simple $A$-module and"}, {"line": 290, "tex": "$\\text{End}_A(M) = K^{op}$."}, {"line": 291, "tex": "\\item If $M$ is a simple $A$-module, then $L = \\text{End}_A(M)$"}, {"line": 292, "tex": "is a skew field finite over $k$ acting on the left on $M$, we have"}, {"line": 293, "tex": "$A = \\text{End}_L(M)$, and the centers of $A$ and $L$ agree."}, {"line": 294, "tex": "Also $[A : k] [L : k] = \\dim_k(M)^2$."}, {"line": 295, "tex": "\\item For a finite $A$-module $N$ the algebra $B = \\text{End}_A(N)$ is a"}, {"line": 296, "tex": "matrix algebra over the skew field $L$ of (5). Moreover $\\text{End}_B(N) = A$."}, {"line": 297, "tex": "\\end{enumerate}"}, {"line": 298, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 320, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 321, "tex": "\\label{lemma-tensor-simple}"}, {"line": 322, "tex": "Let $A$, $A'$ be two simple $k$-algebras one of which is finite and central"}, {"line": 323, "tex": "over $k$. Then $A \\otimes_k A'$ is simple."}, {"line": 324, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 337, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 338, "tex": "\\label{lemma-tensor-central-simple}"}, {"line": 339, "tex": "The tensor product of finite central simple algebras over $k$ is finite,"}, {"line": 340, "tex": "central, and simple."}, {"line": 341, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 347, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 348, "tex": "\\label{lemma-base-change}"}, {"line": 349, "tex": "Let $A$ be a finite central simple algebra over $k$."}, {"line": 350, "tex": "Let $k'/k$ be a field extension. Then $A' = A \\otimes_k k'$ is"}, {"line": 351, "tex": "a finite central simple algebra over $k'$."}, {"line": 352, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}, {"line": 358, "tex": "\\begin{lemma}"}, {"line": 359, "tex": "\\label{lemma-inverse}"}, {"line": 360, "tex": "Let $A$ be a finite central simple algebra over $k$."}, {"line": 361, "tex": "Then $A \\otimes_k A^{op} \\cong \\text{Mat}(n \\times n, k)$"}, {"line": 362, "tex": "where $n = [A : k]$."}, {"line": 363, "tex": "\\end{lemma}"}], "schema": "maththm.phase2.chapter-section-input.v1", "scope_extraction_error_requires_review": null, "section_end_line": 379, "section_label": "section-lemmas", "section_start_line": 166, "section_title": "Lemmas on algebras", "source_file": "brauer.tex", "source_revision": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_scope_events_unadjudicated": [{"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 177, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 177, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 182, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 184, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 192, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 192, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 196, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 198, "scope_stack": []}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "enter_local_environment", "line": 208, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "candidate_location", "line": 208, "scope_stack": ["lemma"]}, {"environment": "lemma", "kind": "exit_local_environment", "line": 214, "persists_after_end": false, "scope_stack_before_pop": ["lemma"]}, {"kind": "proof_skipped", "line": 216, "scope_stack": []}, {"en